  "minute": 119.0,
  "event_seq": 286,
  "root_problem": "Billing import validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, compares raw AMI register values against 12-month m3 history with unit_scaling set to none (E-13); because firmware v4.2 meters, rolled out 2026-06, register consumption in 0.1 m3 units instead of whole m3 (E-14), BV-17 misreads normal v4.2 consumption as abnormally high. This rejected 1184 arriving, exported v4.2 AMI reads as REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION at import (E-12), forcing estimate substitution behind a large share of the 1240 ESTIMATED-type disputed bills (E-02) and coinciding with the August dispute-volume doubling (E-03); the same unit-scaling defect can also miscompute accepted v4.2 ACTUAL-read bills, giving a billing-side mechanism for part of the larger 1785-bill ACTUAL-type dispute share (E-02, E-13, E-14)."
 },
